<title>SLOVENIA: Slovenia bank SKB completes its GDR sale.</title>
<headline>Slovenia bank SKB completes its GDR sale.</headline>
<dateline>LJUBLJANA 1997-02-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Slovenia's second largest bank SKB said on Wednesday it had completed its global depository receipts programme and expected trade in GDRs to start on the London Stock Exchange in the middle of next week.</p>
<p>The GDRs represent 29 percent of SKB's equity and were accepted by the LSE on Monday. A total of 1.3 million GDRs, representing 65,000 ordinary shares, were admitted.</p>
<p>A total of $17.0 million was raised with the issue.</p>
<p>The exchange said SKB was the first Slovenian company to gain a London listing.</p>
<p>-- Ljubljana newsroom, 386-61-125-8439</p>
</text>
